# What never enters the build context.
#
# Two entries here are correctness, not tidiness — read those before editing.

# ─── CORRECTNESS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# `bcrypt` and `sharp` resolve PLATFORM binaries at install time. This tree is
# developed on Windows, so a host `node_modules/` carries `@img/sharp-win32-x64`
# and `bcrypt/prebuilds/win32-x64`. Copying it into a linux image produces a
# container that installs cleanly and then throws at the first hash or resize.
# `npm ci` runs INSIDE the image for exactly this reason; this line is what stops
# a stray `COPY . .` from undoing that.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# 112 MB / 73 files of real uploads. ADR-019 D-1a and plan D-6: they live in a
# named volume mounted at /app/storage, never in an image layer. Without this
# line every build ships them as context AND bakes them into the image, where a
# `docker compose down -v` would be the only thing standing between a rebuild and
# stale files shadowing the volume.
storage

# ─── SECRETS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The real environment. Compose supplies the container's environment and
# `dotenv/config` no-ops when there is no file — that is intended, not a gap.
# `.env.example` is kept: it documents the contract and carries no secret.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── BUILD OUTPUT AND NOISE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The builder stage produces dist/ itself. A host copy would be a Windows-built
# artefact of unknown vintage shadowing it.
dist

.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
coverage

# Documentation. Large, and no code path reads it.
api-doc
docs
*.md
